    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jbacjztk27",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The discussion of AI in gaming is pernicious now. The idea that games are going to be the only field where humans write code unassisted is obviously wrong. But the push for that from press & fans means missing a chance to guide AI usage toward approaches that empower workers & help gaming thrive.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2jbacjztk27",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T14:34:59.037Z",
      "likes": 145,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 20,
      "score": 7.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 6.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2joens5t22x",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I’ve been using GPT-6.2 Astra prior to launch & I found it very uneven  & weird. On one hand, it was harder to steer & work with than other models. On the other, when given an ambitious project (make a space elevator from scratch with Blender & Unity) it delivers upwell-tetherline.netlify.app/unity/",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2joens5t22x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T18:30:03.697Z",
      "likes": 95,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jbackdm227",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Games have always been a very difficult industry with a high cost to its workers in terms of crunch & instability. I would love to see more positive visions about how you rebuild an industry stronger & more fairly using AI, rather than defending the status quo as good and hoping AI is going away.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2jbackdm227",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T14:34:59.038Z",
      "likes": 73,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 6.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2hsler3as2c",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "What an amazing coincidence given the IPO is days away gizmodo.com/anthropic-sa... \nOur progress is accelerating so fast that we need to be extra careful",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2hsler3as2c",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T00:40:04.599Z",
      "likes": 19,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 20.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jltgny2k2t",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "If I were to create the ultimate AI villain, I would create a sandbox simulation for the AI to try to take over the world. I would add an adversary with unrealistic advantages to put pressure on the villain. I would periodically randomly reset the simulation with different starting world conditions.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2jltgny2k2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T17:44:38.315Z",
      "likes": 3,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 4.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.8,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 3.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jfjfcgr22t",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "okay, back at it. The most successful weight editing technique for creating a persona so far is to have Astra implement a FSM inside weight space that adds self-instructions before responding to the prompt. \n\nThe <thinking> tokens below are generated by the FSM portion of the model weights.",
